  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material questioning familial roles",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the text chunk 'is it ok for your son or daughter to call another man \"daddy?\"', which uses the deictic 'your' to directly address the viewer. This creates an implicit 'you' as the subject of the question, making the user feel personally implicated in the moral judgment being posed. The projection is onto the textual material, which frames the viewer as the one who must decide or evaluate the appropriateness of the child's behavior, thereby personalizing the racialized assumption embedded in the meme.",
